/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  ONE tear: the isopropanol recycle, C2's overhead back to the feed mixer.
  It is DECLARED rather than discovered -- the sequential-plan contract
  (settled 2026-07-25) makes cycle DETECTION the engine's job and tear CHOICE
  the author's, and refuses an undeclared backward edge by name.  With one
  cycle there is only one honest cut, and this is it.

  WEGSTEIN, as `recycleSolver` below declares, and MEASURED ON THIS PLANT.
  Newton's Jacobian perturbs the tear five times per iteration and every
  perturbation triggers a full recovery search on C1 -- a nested cost that was
  still grinding after eleven minutes at 200 % CPU.  Wegstein needs one search
  per pass and converged in three (|r| 2.847 -> 2.13e-2 -> 1.785e-4).  The
  case's own CLAUDE.md carries that comparison under `Decisions + why`.

  This paragraph argued the OPPOSITE until 2026-09-24 -- "Newton rather than
  Wegstein", citing acetone03's record that Wegstein was DEFEATED on
  cavett01's conditions while Newton took 7 iterations -- six lines above a
  declaration that says Wegstein.  The file told a reader one thing and the
  engine did another, and the prose was the false half: acetone03's finding
  was made on a different flowsheet, and this one was measured directly.
  A solver aid is the student's to see, so the reason lives here.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
tearStreams    ( ipaRecycle );
recycleSolver  Wegstein;
recycleTol     1e-6;
recycleMaxIter 120;
